    "For POST /orders the request body is untrusted and may be too large or invalid. Limit its size before decoding JSON: MaxBytesReader returns *http.MaxBytesError when a read exceeds the limit; detect it with errors.As and return 413. Return 400 for malformed JSON. Pass r.Context() to storage that supports cancellation. The context is cancelled on disconnect, HTTP/2 request cancellation, or handler return; do not replace it with Background() for request work. This lesson checks code fragments rather than executing Go.",
